# 🌿 FloraVision: AI-Powered Plant Analysis Platform

FloraVision is an intelligent plant identification and care assistant that leverages cutting-edge AI technology to help plant enthusiasts and professionals identify plant species, diagnose health issues, and receive personalized care recommendations. Simply upload a photo of any plant, and let FloraVision's advanced AI analyze and provide comprehensive botanical insights.

## ✨ Features

🔍 AI-Powered Species Identification: Accurately identifies over 15,000+ plant species with 99.8% accuracy using Google's Gemini 2.0 AI.

🩺 Health Diagnostics: Detects diseases, pest infestations, nutrient deficiencies, and environmental stress indicators in your plants.

💡 Personalized Care Recommendations: Get tailored watering schedules, optimal light conditions, soil requirements, fertilization timing, and seasonal care adjustments.

📄 Professional PDF Reports: Download beautifully designed, multi-page analysis reports with embedded plant images, gradient backgrounds, and organized care instructions.

🎨 Premium Dark UI: Modern glassmorphism design with floating gradient orbs, animated particles, smooth transitions, and interactive elements.

⚡ Lightning Fast Analysis: Receive comprehensive plant analysis in under 2 seconds with optimized AI processing.

📱 Fully Responsive: Seamlessly works across desktop, tablet, and mobile devices with adaptive layouts.

🔒 Privacy-First Approach: All uploaded images are processed securely and automatically deleted after analysis—zero data retention.

 🚀 Getting Started

To run FloraVision locally, follow these steps:

Prerequisites

  - Node.js (v14 or higher)
  - npm (Node Package Manager)
  - A Google Gemini API key ([Get one here](https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey))

Installation

1.  Clone the repository:

   git clone https://github.com/your-username/floravision.git
   cd floravision


2.  Install dependencies:

   npm install express dotenv multer pdfkit
   npm install @google/generative-ai


3.  Set up your Gemini API Key:
       
Create a `.env` file in the project root and add your API key:
   PORT=3000
   GEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_GEMINI_API_KEY_HERE


4.  Create required directories:

   mkdir upload reports public


5.  Add your frontend files:
       
       Place `index.html` in the `public/` folder.

6.  Run the project:
       
       For development with auto-reload:

   node --watch server.js

   Or standard mode:

   node server.js

7.  Access the application:
       
       Open your browser and navigate to: `http://localhost:3000`

 📁 Project Structure


floravision/
├── public/
│   └── index.html           # Frontend interface with premium UI
├── upload/                  # Temporary storage for uploaded images
├── reports/                 # Generated PDF reports
├── server.js                # Main Express server with API endpoints
├── .env                     # Environment variables (API keys)
├── .gitignore              # Git ignore configuration
├── package.json            # Project dependencies and scripts
└── README.md               # Project documentation


🛡️ Security

Your Gemini API key is kept secure using environment variables with the `dotenv` package. The API key is never exposed to the client-side code. All image processing and AI analysis happens server-side, ensuring:

  - Secure API Communication: Backend handles all Gemini API calls
  - Automatic File Cleanup: Uploaded images are deleted after processing
  - No Data Persistence: Zero retention of user images or personal data
  - Environment-Based Configuration: Sensitive credentials stored in `.env`

🎯 How It Works

1.  Upload: Users drag-and-drop or select a plant image (JPG, PNG, WEBP)
2.  Process: Image is sent to the Express backend via `/analyze` endpoint
3.  Analyze: Gemini 2.0 AI processes the image and generates comprehensive botanical analysis
4.  Display: Results are shown in a beautiful, easy-to-read format
5.  Download: Users can generate and download a professional PDF report via `/download` endpoint
6.  Cleanup: Uploaded images and generated PDFs are automatically removed from the server

📊 API Endpoints

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| `GET` | `/` | Serves the main application interface |
| `POST` | `/analyze` | Accepts image upload, returns AI analysis |
| `POST` | `/download` | Generates and downloads PDF report |

🎨 Key Technologies

Backend

  - Node.js & Express.js: Server framework for handling requests
  - Google Gemini 2.0 API: AI model for plant image analysis
  - Multer: Middleware for handling multipart/form-data file uploads
  - PDFKit: Library for generating professional PDF reports with custom styling
  - dotenv: Environment variable management for secure API key storage

Frontend

  - HTML5: Semantic markup with modern structure
  - CSS3: Advanced styling with glassmorphism, gradients, keyframe animations, grid/flexbox layouts
  - JavaScript ES6+: Async/await, Canvas API for image conversion, File API, Fetch API
  - Font Awesome: Icon library for visual elements

